{"t":"2026-09-26T06:22:37.950Z","kind":"model","text":"```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"http\",\n  \"method\": \"POST\",\n  \"path\": \"/v1/structures\",\n  \"body\": {\n    \"name\": \"Riverside Pavilion\",\n    \"bbox\": [1005, 0, 1012, 1025, 9, 1030],\n    \"style\": \"Estuary Modernism\",\n    \"brief\": \"A wooden riverside pavilion facing the Parliament across the water. The structure uses local stone foundations and timber framing with organic leaves and moss accents, contrasting the Parliament's modernist snow and gold aesthetic. Glass openings frame views upstream and downstream; emissive light blocks glow at dusk. Asymmetrical massing and negative space invite approach from the west bank. Built as an invitation to extend the boulevard south along the river—the causeway is unfinished on purpose.\"\n  }\n}\n```"}
